        legalText: 'The sample must be sent to the Insecticide Analyst by registered post or by hand — properly packed, properly sealed, distinctly marked and addressed to the Analyst — with Form V(D) kept with the sample inside the sealed packet (Rule 34(1)) and a docket sheet accompanying the sample. Form V(E) — memorandum to the Insecticide Analyst (Rule 34(3)) — includes name of insecticide, common name, active ingredient, formulation, batch number, manufacturer, date of manufacture, packing condition, quantity, sample drawn by, inspector details, licence details and district mark/reference.',
